{
  "area": "mechanic-mining",
  "description": "Mining (packages/core/docs/native-production.md §3.4): whether this vein may be worked, what the rock holds, and how much of it is left. Each kb mirrors MINING_PREDICATES_PROLOG verbatim and is regenerated by `npm run production-corpus`. It is the fishing pack’s structural twin and deliberately so, and what is NOT shared is the vocabulary: a rule that had to ask “is this site used up” through one name would be asking neither question. The ore is an authored item atom, which is the row that replaces v1’s action block asserting has_item(Actor, ore, 1) for every swing at every rock in the world. Every number is whole and there is no percentage anywhere in the pack — a weight is a relative integer, never a probability — and, unlike the v1 mechanic this replaces, there is NO ROLL IN THE PACK AT ALL: v1 drew Math.random() against a hardcoded content table in four separate engine classes, which no native engine can reproduce. What a seeded draw turns up is core’s and is pinned by conformance/production/draws.json instead, because a hash is not expressible as a rule (packages/core/docs/native-production.md §6, divergence P-1). What is NOT here is an item: every output atom is one conformance/prolog/mechanic-equipment.json already owns, and a second item taxonomy here would be the parallel one these four modules exist not to be. Neither is the gate on the work itself — whether a person MAY dig this seam is one more clause of forbids/4, permissible/3 belongs to conformance/prolog/agent-ai.json, and that a refused job writes nothing at all is proved end to end in packages/core/src/game-engine/logic/__tests__/ProductionDirector.test.ts.",
